From: U2W build
Subject: [PATCH] aacdec: bound the error-path output clear to one frame and timeDataSize bytes

0.1.5 moved decoding into the internal pcmOutputBuffer and, when a call
returns no valid output (IS_OUTPUT_VALID false: AAC_DEC_NOT_ENOUGH_BITS,
TRANSPORT_SYNC_ERROR, NEED_TO_RESTART, UNKNOWN, OUTPUT_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL,
init/unsupported errors), clears the caller buffer with
  FDKmemclear(pTimeData_extern, timeDataSize_extern*sizeof(INT_PCM));
0.1.4 (the vendor library) never wrote the caller buffer on that path.

AppleCarPlay passes timeDataSize in BYTES (its mDataByteSize), with a buffer
of channelConfig*aacSamplesPerFrame*2 bytes, so the upstream clear writes
twice the buffer: a heap overflow on every DecodeFrame call that returns an
error (e.g. NOT_ENOUGH_BITS after a short/missing packet).

Audit of every write to pTimeData_extern / use of timeDataSize_extern in
0.1.6 aacDecoder_DecodeFrame (all other decoding writes only the internal
pcmOutputBuffer, sized by sizeof(self->pcmOutputBuffer)):
 1. timeDataSize_extern < numChannels*frameSize -> OUTPUT_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL:
    a samples-vs-bytes check; for a byte-counting caller it is laxer, never
    stricter, so it cannot reject AppleCarPlay frames.
 2. valid output: memcpy of numChannels*frameSize samples -- exactly the
    samples 0.1.4 decoded in place into the same buffer, so no write beyond
    what the vendor library already did for the same stream.
 3. invalid output: the clear fixed here.

The clear now covers at most one frame (numChannels*frameSize samples, the
footprint of path 2) and at most timeDataSize_extern bytes, so it stays
inside the buffer whether the caller counts samples or bytes.  Callers that
pass samples still get the whole frame region zeroed whenever their buffer
holds two frames' worth of samples, otherwise its first timeDataSize bytes;
output is undefined on these errors anyway (0.1.4 left it untouched), and
AppleCarPlay itself zeroes channelConfig*aacSamplesPerFrame*2 bytes on error.
Before the first decoded frame numChannels*frameSize is 0 and nothing is
written, as in 0.1.4.

--- a/libAACdec/src/aacdecoder_lib.cpp
+++ b/libAACdec/src/aacdecoder_lib.cpp
@@ -1062,7 +1062,16 @@
       FDKmemcpy(pTimeData_extern, pTimeData, self->streamInfo.numChannels*self->streamInfo.frameSize*sizeof(*pTimeData));
     }
     else {
-      FDKmemclear(pTimeData_extern, timeDataSize_extern*sizeof(*pTimeData_extern));
+      /* Clear no more than one decoded frame, and no more than timeDataSize_extern
+         bytes: callers that pass the buffer size in bytes instead of samples
+         (fdk-aac <= 0.1.4 never wrote on this path) must not be overrun. */
+      INT clearBytes = self->streamInfo.numChannels*self->streamInfo.frameSize*(INT)sizeof(*pTimeData_extern);
+      if (clearBytes > timeDataSize_extern) {
+        clearBytes = timeDataSize_extern;
+      }
+      if (clearBytes > 0) {
+        FDKmemclear(pTimeData_extern, clearBytes);
+      }
     }
 
     return ErrorStatus;
